OL,3,GNEWSABaby's 'life-changing' early
OL,4,Adiagnosis in study
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mother has said the early diagnosis
OL,7,Fof her baby boy's rare immune condition
OL,8,Fthrough a genetic study has been
OL,9,F"life-changing".
OL,11,FElaine Hess's son Aidan was born at
OL,12,FRoyal Derby Hospital on 17 October last
OL,13,Fyear, and, as part of the national
OL,14,FGeneration Study, a sample was taken
OL,15,Ffrom the umbilical cord and tested for
OL,16,Fmore than 200 rare, treatable genetic
OL,17,Fconditions.
OL,19,FA few weeks later, she received a call
OL,20,Fto say a possible immune condition
OL,21,Faffecting the body's ability to fight
OL,22,Finfection had been identified.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,362,360,200,160,0,100
